"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,610\nThe Learning Brain. Series 8: Assessment That Teaches\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,435\nEpisode 12\n\n3\n00:00:07,515 --> 00:00:10,220\nDesigning assessment that teaches\n\n4\n00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:20,093\nAcross this series, one idea has run through every episode: assessment is not only how we measure learning.\n\n5\n00:00:20,537 --> 00:00:23,105\nDone well, it is how learning happens.\n\n6\n00:00:23,452 --> 00:00:28,338\nThis episode pulls the whole series together into one simple plan for a unit: before,\n\n7\n00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:30,662\nduring and after.\n\n8\n00:00:30,832 --> 00:00:31,849\nBefore a unit.\n\n9\n00:00:32,335 --> 00:00:35,297\nPose a few pretest questions to focus attention.\n\n10\n00:00:35,679 --> 00:00:40,447\nMake the purpose, task and criteria of each assignment transparent,\n\n11\n00:00:40,593 --> 00:00:42,429\nwith an example of good work.\n\n12\n00:00:42,599 --> 00:00:43,270\nDuring.\n\n13\n00:00:43,316 --> 00:00:45,193\nQuiz often, low stakes,\n\n14\n00:00:45,409 --> 00:00:49,297\nwith questions that require recall and plausible wrong answers.\n\n15\n00:00:49,736 --> 00:00:51,827\nGive feedback that says what to do next,\n\n16\n00:00:51,847 --> 00:00:53,340\nand leave room to use it.\n\n17\n00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:54,149\nAfter.\n\n18\n00:00:54,224 --> 00:00:56,527\nMake later exams cumulative,\n\n19\n00:00:56,608 --> 00:00:58,285\nso earlier material comes back.\n\n20\n00:00:58,838 --> 00:01:02,042\nOffer retakes or revisions on key outcomes,\n\n21\n00:01:02,086 --> 00:01:03,822\nwith new learning in between.\n\n22\n00:01:04,236 --> 00:01:05,980\nAnd design for integrity,\n\n23\n00:01:06,002 --> 00:01:07,552\nwith visible process.\n\n24\n00:01:07,722 --> 00:01:08,701\nSome caution.\n\n25\n00:01:09,037 --> 00:01:11,233\nNot every popular practice holds up.\n\n26\n00:01:11,631 --> 00:01:14,937\nExam wrappers, short reflections after a test,\n\n27\n00:01:15,139 --> 00:01:19,515\nshowed no effect on grades in one well designed single course study.\n\n28\n00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:22,886\nSpecifications grading has mixed evidence.\n\n29\n00:01:23,182 --> 00:01:25,361\nCheck what happens in your own course.\n\n30\n00:01:25,531 --> 00:01:28,214\nNone of this needs a full course redesign.\n\n31\n00:01:28,626 --> 00:01:29,854\nEach change is small,\n\n32\n00:01:29,874 --> 00:01:32,629\nand each one can be tried in a single unit.\n\n33\n00:01:33,155 --> 00:01:38,692\nThe thread through all of it is simple: the more an assessment asks students to retrieve,\n\n34\n00:01:38,712 --> 00:01:41,380\nthink and improve, the more it teaches.\n\n35\n00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:42,375\nFor teaching.\n\n36\n00:01:42,714 --> 00:01:44,192\nPick one change for before,\n\n37\n00:01:44,212 --> 00:01:46,139\nduring and after your next unit.\n\n38\n00:01:46,555 --> 00:01:48,562\nTell students why you are making it.\n\n39\n00:01:48,879 --> 00:01:51,446\nThen look at what they learned,\n\n40\n00:01:51,783 --> 00:01:53,707\nand keep what works.\n\n41\n00:01:53,957 --> 00:01:56,675\nOne tip to share with students: use every test as practice for the next one.\n\n42\n00:01:56,845 --> 00:01:58,840\nEvery test is a chance to learn.\n\n43\n00:01:59,074 --> 00:02:00,240\nDesign it that way.\n\n44\n00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:02,269\nThanks for watching series eight.\n\n"